# EdgeDesk process supervisor for BusyBox init.
#
# Install as an /etc/inittab entry (or append to an existing inittab) and run
# `kill -HUP 1` after changing it. BusyBox respawns the Supervisor if it exits;
# the Supervisor itself remains responsible for the managed services.
#
# /usr/sbin/edgedesk-supervisor-boot creates its private state and log
# directories with the required modes before exec'ing the daemon.
#
# The console is the Supervisor's stdout/stderr. On a device without a serial
# console attach the output to syslog or a file with a small wrapper.
::respawn:/usr/sbin/edgedesk-supervisor-boot
